Chapter: RealNegNeg

 Double negation on a Real.

 `IrNegate` carried no type field, so a backend that needed to know
 whether a negation was floating-point had to ask the OPERAND. The
 compiler's `ir-expr-type` answered a negation by recursing into its
 operand; the plug's copy answered `int-ty-default`. The two disagreed
 exactly when the operand of a negation was itself a negation, and then
 the plug integer negated an IEEE double's bit pattern.

 The node carries a `CodexType` now, lowering fills it, and the text
 wire sends it, so no backend re-derives it and there is no second
 answer to disagree with. This test is the repro that found the
 divergence and it stays: it is what would see the field stop being
 filled.

Section: The Forms

  neg-neg : Real -> Real
  neg-neg (x) = -(-x)

  neg-neg-call : Real -> Real
  neg-neg-call (x) = -(-(x * 2.0))

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("neg-neg      " & show (real-to-int (neg-neg 2.5 * 10.0)))
    print-line-uni ("neg-neg-call " & show (real-to-int (neg-neg-call 2.5 * 10.0)))
  end
